 the maximum-likelihood s.d.\ of a random walk from 2014 observed at \(h=2,3,4\); the growth-based values replace \(n_t\) with \(n_t-n_{2015}\) and count \(h\) from 2015. The Netflix-derived value applies only when it exceeds the series' historical volatility.
 
+\subsection*{Integrating over the error scale (post hoc)}
+
+The priors and what to report were fixed in \texttt{DECISIONS.md} before the first version below was computed. With a flat prior on \(k\) and \(\Omega\) the matrix with entries \(\min(h_s,h_t)\), integrating \(k\) out of the likelihood leaves
+\[
+p(y\mid\sigma)\propto\sigma^{-3}\operatorname{exp}\bigl(-\mathrm{RSS}/2\sigma^2\bigr),\qquad \mathrm{RSS}=y'\Omega^{-1}y-(\delta'\Omega^{-1}y)^2/\delta'\Omega^{-1}\delta,
+\]
+and given \(\sigma\), \(k\) is normal with mean \(\hat k\) and variance \(\sigma^2/\delta'\Omega^{-1}\delta\) \citep[372]{GelmanBDA3}. The first prior on \(\sigma\) is uniform on the plan's sensitivity range, 1\% to 8\% a year. The second treats the report's 2010--2014 volatility \(s\) as an estimate from four annual changes: \(\sigma^2\) is scaled-inverse-\(\chi^2\) with 3 degrees of freedom and scale \(s^2\). In the version specified first, \(\sigma\)'s posterior combines its prior with \(p(y\mid\sigma)\); in the prior-only version, computed after it, the likelihood term is dropped and \(\sigma\)'s posterior is its prior. In both, the posterior for \(k\) is a mixture of normals over \(\sigma\), computed on a grid from 0.1\% to 20\% a year in steps of 0.01 points and checked against 400,000 Monte Carlo draws. Extending the grid to 100\% a year moves no 95\% end by more than \lttvKIntGridShiftMax{}; the largest move is in the prior-only distributors' interval under the history-based prior, whose lower end, \lttvKIntBDUHistOnlyLoThree{} (0.00 in table~\ref{tab:calibrations}), becomes \lttvKIntBDUHistOnlyLoWide{}. In the version specified first, the 50\% intervals are \lttvKIntSpecUnifLoFifty{} to \lttvKIntSpecUnifHiFifty{} (specialty and pay) and \lttvKIntBDUUnifLoFifty{} to \lttvKIntBDUUnifHiFifty{} (distributors) under the uniform prior, and \lttvKIntSpecHistLoFifty{} to \lttvKIntSpecHistHiFifty{} and \lttvKIntBDUHistLoFifty{} to \lttvKIntBDUHistHiFifty{} with the volatility as data. The band doesn't depend on \(\sigma\). Produced by \texttt{scripts/sigma\_integrated\_lttv.py}; data in \texttt{data/derived/sigma\_integrated\_lttv.csv}.
+
 \section{Tables}
 \label{app:tables}
 
